    {
      "id": "sol.hmmt-feb-calculus-2004-p6.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "1\nLet \\(g(x)=\\log f(x)=x \\log x\\). Then \\(f^{\\prime}(x) / f(x)=g^{\\prime}(x)=1+\\log x\\). Therefore \\(f(x)=f^{\\prime}(x)\\) when \\(1+\\log x=1\\), that is, when \\(x=1\\).",
